# Page layout below fixed header

The site header is fixed (announcement bar + nav). Page content must not sit under it.

## Use these exports from `@/components/storefront/ui`

| Export | When to use |
|--------|-------------|
| `PageMain` | Default wrapper for new `page.tsx` routes |
| `SECTION_PADDING_BELOW_HEADER` | Sections inside home or catalog blocks (includes px + pb + offset) |
| `HEADER_OFFSET_TOP` | Custom shells (help layout, centered error/offline) |

Offsets: `pt-[calc(84px+2.5rem)] lg:pt-[calc(121px+4rem)]` (84px / 121px header stack + section rhythm).

## New pages

```tsx
import { PageMain } from '@/components/storefront/ui';

export default function MyPage() {
  return (
    <PageMain>
      {/* content */}
    </PageMain>
  );
}
```

- **Hero band inside the page** (dark header block): `<PageMain padded={false}>`
- **Centered utility page** (login): `<PageMain padded={false} className="flex items-center justify-center bg-gray-50">`
- **Help / legal content**: use `HelpPageLayout` (offset built in)

## Exceptions — do NOT add header offset

- **Home** (`/[locale]`): hero is full-bleed under the transparent header; uses `Hero` height calc instead.
- **Nested sections on home**: use `SECTION_PADDING_BELOW_HEADER` only when needed below the hero.

## Do not

- Duplicate `pt-[calc(84px…)]` literals — use `HEADER_OFFSET_TOP` or `PageMain`.
- Wrap home content in `PageMain`.
- Nest `<main>` inside layout; locale layout uses `<div>`; each page owns `<main>` via `PageMain`.
